                                   "title":  "Wikipedia: Tokyo Ueno Station (novel)",
                                   "snippet":  "[Wikipedia Synopsis] Tokyo Ueno Station (Japanese: JR上野駅公園口, Hepburn: JR Ueno-Eki Kōenguchi) is a 2014 novel by Zainichi Korean author Yū Miri.\nThe novel reflects the author\u0027s engagement with historical memory and margins by incorporating themes of a migrant laborer from northeastern Japan and his work on Olympic construction sites in Tokyo, as well as the 11 March 2011 disaster. In November 2020, Tokyo Ueno Station won the National Book Award for Translated Literature for the English translation by translator Morgan Giles.",
                                   "link":  "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tokyo%20Ueno%20Station%20(novel)"
                               }
